          "en": "some normal CSS styling, nothing angular specific",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.97,
          "end": 74.283,
          "en": "and our app looks a little bit nicer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.429,
          "end": 76.83,
          "en": "Now this is great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.83,
          "end": 81.33,
          "en": "but we can also use some tools given to us by angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.33,
          "end": 84.9,
          "en": "Let's say this, I'm in the AppComponent heading here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.9,
          "end": 87.39,
          "en": "We want to change its style.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.39,
          "end": 92.16,
          "en": "Maybe we want to give the some blue color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.16,
          "end": 95.91,
          "en": "We can do it as by going to the AppComponent CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.91,
          "end": 99.72,
          "en": "which defines the styling for this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.72,
          "end": 103.563,
          "en": "And now we can use or write normal CSS code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.563,
          "end": 105.7,
          "en": "So override the style of the H three tag",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.932,
          "end": 109.47,
          "en": "and set its color to some blue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.47,
          "end": 113.1,
          "en": "So maybe to this dark blue here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.1,
          "end": 115.269,
          "en": "If we now save this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.269,
          "end": 116.187,
          "en": "And we have a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.187,
          "end": 120.06,
          "en": "at our application, you see it's dark blue now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.06,
          "end": 123.12,
          "en": "this is how you can use this style file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.12,
          "end": 127.617,
          "en": "this CSS file referenced in the App Component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.617,
          "end": 131.4,
          "en": "to define the styles for a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.4,
          "end": 135.27,
          "en": "Now just like we were able to choose between external file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.27,
          "end": 140.27,
          "en": "and inline code for the template, we can do the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.57999999999998,
          "end": 142.47,
          "en": "for the styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.47,
          "end": 145.86,
          "en": "You notice that style URLs is an array here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.86,
          "end": 148.23,
          "en": "where as template URL wasn't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.23,
          "end": 151.14,
          "en": "It is this because we could reference multiple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.14,
          "end": 152.85,
          "en": "external style sheets here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.85,
          "end": 156.69,
          "en": "So you could add pointers to other style sheets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.69,
          "end": 160.29,
          "en": "But besides that, I'm going to comment this out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.29,
          "end": 164.1,
          "en": "You can also set up another property, which is just styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.1,
          "end": 167.799,
          "en": "This also takes an array, but now it takes an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 167.799,
          "end": 170.7,
          "en": "of strings where you define the style in this string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.7,
          "end": 175.526,
          "en": "So now in this file here, I'm going to use backticks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.526,
          "end": 177.77,
          "en": "again to be able to write a multi-line expression here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 177.77,
          "end": 178.82999999999998,
          "en": "And then we could",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 178.82999999999998,
          "end": 180.66,
          "en": "-: Set up H three here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.66,
          "end": 183.21,
          "en": "And to really show you that this is different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.21,
          "end": 185.55,
          "en": "I will set a color to now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.55,
          "end": 190.55,
          "en": "let's not say dark blue, but to dodger blue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 190.65,
          "end": 194.46,
          "en": "And if I now save this and we go back to the application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 194.46,
          "end": 196.32,
          "en": "you see the blue updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 196.32,
          "end": 199.38,
          "en": "because now the inline style is taking over.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 199.38,
          "end": 201.153,
          "en": "I commented out the other one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.05,
          "end": 203.37,
          "en": "Just like with the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 203.37,
          "end": 205.35,
          "en": "you have to decide which one to use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.35,
          "end": 207.451,
          "en": "You can't combine style URLs and styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 207.451,
          "end": 210.831,
          "en": "but both important here has to be an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 210.831,
          "end": 212.94,
          "en": "That's the different to template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 212.94,
          "end": 214.77,
          "en": "You must only have one template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 214.77,
          "end": 218.279,
          "en": "You may have multiple style files or style definitions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 218.279,
          "end": 223.23,
          "en": "and you can choose between inline and external file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 223.23,
          "end": 226.23,
          "en": "The rules are basically the same as for template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 226.23,
          "end": 228.69,
          "en": "If you have more code in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 228.69,
          "end": 231.27,
          "en": "using an external file is a good idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 231.27,
          "end": 233.64,
          "en": "If it's a short style definition like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 233.64,
          "end": 236.85,
          "en": "why don't you just put it into the TypeScript file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 236.85,
          "end": 240.063,
          "en": "This is how you can work with templates and styles.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
